# Regenerated by `next dev` on every run (next.config's `agentRules`).
# `next-env.d.ts` stays tracked — Next's docs say to commit that one.
# Next writes two variants of it: `next build` references ./.next/types/…
# and `next dev` references ./.next/dev/types/…. The build variant is what
# is committed (CI builds); after running the dev server the file shows as
# modified — that is expected, discard it rather than committing it.
